Apple Blocks (-fblocks) for C and Objective-C, with the PLBlocks runtime.

Port of https://github.com/Jazzzny/gcc-13-branch-panther/commit/6859619c9718b8f61df6a45188d50475ed8d5264
("Add the PLBlocks runtime", GCC 13) to GCC 16.  Made against
https://github.com/iains/gcc-16-branch gcc-16-2-darwin-pre-0
(97f8cc058fcb386fda01ccba81202131bd8637c8); apply with -p0 after
patch-darwin-gcc-16.2.0.diff.

libplblocks/ vendors the PLBlocks runtime from the Google Code archive
(Runtime/trunk r219, the last runtime change; later revisions only touch
compiler packaging).  It is built as a target library and installed as
libPLBlocks.{1.dylib,a}.  -fblocks selects the PLBlocks ABI and links
-lPLBlocks for deployment targets older than 10.6, and the system Blocks
runtime for 10.6 and later; -fblocks-runtime=plblocks|system overrides.

Changes relative to the GCC 13 commit:
 - rebased onto the GCC 16 C front end (comptypes_data, new argument-count
   diagnostics, grokdeclarator arg spec rework, mark_decl_used);
 - Jazzzny's -ObjC/-ObjC++ driver options dropped: Iain's branch already
   provides them in config/darwin.opt;
 - top-level Makefile.in regenerated for the GCC 16 template (adds the
   default libatomic configure dependency);
 - caches of shared trees made GC roots (c_block_trees in c-lang.h);
 - helpers synthesized for file-scope block literals are static, so
   several objects with global blocks can be linked together;
 - the PLBlocks header is installed as <PLBlocks/Block.h>; <Block.h>
   selects it only when __PLBLOCKS__ is defined (new, set for
   -fblocks-runtime=plblocks) and otherwise uses the SDK's <Block.h>;
 - documentation moved under "Syntax Extensions"; tests updated for
   GCC 16 (-Wincompatible-pointer-types is a permerror).

