+@opindex fblocks
+@item -fblocks
+Enable Apple Blocks syntax and ABI lowering in C and Objective-C.
+This defines @code{__BLOCKS__}, recognizes block pointer declarators and
+block literals, and makes @code{__block} available as a mutable-capture
+storage qualifier.  @xref{Apple Blocks}.
+
+@opindex fblocks-runtime
+@item -fblocks-runtime=@var{runtime}
+Select the external Blocks runtime ABI.  On Darwin, @option{-fblocks}
+defaults to @code{plblocks} for deployment targets older than macOS 10.6
+and to @code{system} for macOS 10.6 and later.  An explicit
+@option{-fblocks-runtime=} option overrides that deployment-target default.
+The value @code{system} emits references to Apple's
+@code{_NSConcrete@dots{}} classes and @code{_Block_object_@dots{}} ownership
+functions.  The value
+@code{plblocks} emits PLBlocks' collision-safe prefixed references and links
+@code{libPLBlocks} when GCC performs the final Darwin link; it also
+defines the preprocessor macro @code{__PLBLOCKS__}.  PLBlocks is
+intended as a compatibility runtime for macOS releases before 10.6.
+
