+PLBlocks source provenance
+**************************
+
+This directory contains a preserved copy of the PLBlocks runtime.
+PLBlocks is an archived project and is no longer maintained upstream.
+
+The imported sources are retained as part of this GCC port.  They are
+not intended to track a continuing upstream development branch.
+
+
+Upstream source
+===============
+
+The imported runtime has the following provenance:
+
+        Project:                 PLBlocks
+        Archived repository:    http://plblocks.googlecode.com/svn
+        Imported path:          Runtime/trunk
+        Working-copy revision:  224
+        Last-changed revision:   219
+        Last-changed date:       2011-04-10
+        Last-changed author:     landon.j.fuller
+
+The complete Google Code source archive is available at:
+
+        https://storage.googleapis.com/google-code-archive-source/v2/code.google.com/plblocks/source-archive.zip
+
+The SHA-256 digest of that archive is:
+
+        40c8912264fb3314aff81a4bf09f2b96a2b48f47e20d086626f90e5a04de9ec1
+
+The sources are distributed under the Blocks Runtime License, an
+MIT-style license.  A copy is included in `LICENSE'.
+
+
+Imported files
+==============
+
+The files in `src' are derived from the revision 219 Mac OS X runtime
+sources.
+
+The files in `config' are derived from the revision 219 Mac OS X linker
+alias lists.
+
+Four files in the archived source did not end with a newline.  A final
+newline was added to the imported copies of:
+
+        NSBlock.h
+        NSBlock.m
+        config/objc1_symbol_aliases.txt
+        config/objc2_symbol_aliases.txt
+
+No functional change is intended by these newline additions.
+
+The hashes recorded in `SHA256SUMS' identify the upstream-derived files
+included in this directory.
+
+
+Local source adaptation
+=======================
+
+There is one local source adaptation.
+
+The original `Block.m' and `NSBlock.m' referred directly to six optional
+entry points in Apple's Blocks runtime by means of weak imports.  The
+original PLBlocks project was linked against the Mac OS X 10.6 SDK,
+where those symbols were known to the linker.
+
+This GCC port must also build the runtime against the Mac OS X 10.5 SDK.
+With that SDK, direct calls to the weak runtime functions produce
+unresolved lazy stubs.  The Mac OS X 10.5 dynamic loader attempts to
+resolve those stubs while loading the library and terminates the
+program before `main' is entered.
+
+The local versions of `Block.m' and `NSBlock.m' locate the six optional
+Apple runtime hooks with `dlsym' instead.
+
+The lookup is performed through function pointers.  This preserves the
+original PLBlocks behavior on Mac OS X 10.6 and later, where operations
+may be passed to Apple's Blocks runtime, while avoiding references to
+unavailable Apple symbols in a library built for Mac OS X 10.5.
+
+
+Material not imported
+=====================
+
+The following parts of the archived PLBlocks project are deliberately
+not included.
+
+Patched compiler trees
+----------------------
+
+The patched GCC 4.2 and LLVM compiler trees are omitted.  This
+repository carries its compiler changes independently in the GCC source
+tree.
+
+Development and packaging files
+-------------------------------
+
+The Xcode projects, installer packages, and compiler plug-ins are
+omitted.  They are not used by the GCC target-library build.
+
+Obsolete mobile implementations
+--------------------------------
+
+The iPhone OS and simulator assembly sources and concrete block-class
+implementations are omitted.
+
+Those files were written for obsolete ARMv6 and i386 mobile targets and
+are not used by the supported Darwin configurations in this GCC port.
+
+Original test harness
+---------------------
+
+The SenTestingKit and Google Toolbox test harness is omitted.
+
+The relevant C, Objective-C, and C++ behavior is covered by tests
+adapted for the GCC and libplblocks test harnesses.
+
+
+Choice of upstream revision
+===========================
+
+The runtime trunk at revision 219 is used instead of the PLBlocks beta7
+tag.
+
+Revision 219 contains the final bit-29 definition of `BLOCK_USE_STRET'.
+That definition is the form expected by Apple's later Blocks compilers
+and runtimes.
+
+
+Archival status
+===============
+
+This copy of PLBlocks is treated as archived third-party source.
+
+The original project is no longer active, and no future upstream
+releases are expected.  Local changes should be limited to those needed
+for GCC integration, supported legacy Darwin targets, build-system
+compatibility, and correction of defects found in this port.
